sks losing initiative early if peasants have a 2 or joker.  \n4. **Bomb ♠2 ♥2 ♣2 ♦2** – very aggressive, immediately reduces hand by 4 cards and establishes dominance, but bombs are best saved to regain control later or secure the win; using it now leaves me vulnerable if peasants have rockets or higher bombs later.\n\n**Reason:**  \nThe best opening is a **straight** because:  \n- It plays out 5 cards in one go, significantly reducing hand size.  \n- The straight ♣6 ♦7 ♠8 ♣9 ♣10 is not too high, so peasants are less likely to beat it immediately.  \n- After playing this straight, I keep all my 2s, joker, and strong pairs (KK, AA, and mid pairs) for later control.  \n- This move retains flexibility: I still have the bomb, Black Joker, and several 2s to regain control if peasants try to take over.  \n\nBy contrast, starting with a pair or single uses fewer cards and may give peasants a chance to play more freely. The bomb is too precious to use in the opening.\n\n**Answer:** {"cards": ["♣6", "♦7", "♠8", "♣9", "♣10"]}'}
